# Line endings for GENERATED files (PP6b, 2026-08-15).
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, so git rewrites
# checked-out files to CRLF. That is fine for hand-edited source — but a file
# produced by a script is compared against what the script produces, and the
# script writes LF. Without this, `docs/content-v2-spec.json` shows up as
# modified the instant it is regenerated after any checkout, and a re-run looks
# unstable when it is byte-identical. PP6c re-runs the extractor over all 22
# focus areas and diffs the result, so a phantom diff there would be genuinely
# misleading rather than merely untidy.
#
# Pinned narrowly, to generated artefacts only. Ordinary source keeps the
# repo's existing behaviour.
docs/content-v2-spec.json     text eol=lf
docs/content-v2-manifest.json text eol=lf
